On Sun, 9 Jan 2005 jasonnorthrup@yahoo.com wrote:

> for realism, up staircases could be generated with one square of wall
> NSEW adjacent to them, though it might present a problem if this
> blocked a path, or made it necessary to travel diagonally along a path.

In NetHack, "realism" and "staircases" (or any kind of vertical
connectivity) do not match. Introducing such a block (which would
represent the space on which the stair ends on the upper level, I presume)
would only exemplify this further, because it would be another connection
of sequential levels, which NetHack does not really model.

